{"name":"Ahoy","hex":"#2a3149","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ahoy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Used to hail a ship, a boat or a person, or to attract attention.","Warning of something approaching or impending."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hail with a cry of \"ahoy\"."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ahoy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ahoy","blocks":[{"text":"Ahoy is a signal word used to call to a ship or boat. It is derived from the Middle English cry, 'Hoy!'. The word fell out of use at one time, but was revived when sailing became a popular sport. 'Ahoy' can also be used as a greeting, a warning, or a farewell."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahoy"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Piers_plowman_drolleries.gif/250px-Piers_plowman_drolleries.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/53/Piers_plowman_drolleries.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Piers_plowman_drolleries.gif/250px-Piers_plowman_drolleries.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Piers the Plowman, driving oxen, in a Psalter from the 14th century","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APiers_plowman_drolleries.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Oxf_ahoy_smollett_1751.jpg/500px-Oxf_ahoy_smollett_1751.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Oxf_ahoy_smollett_1751.jpg/1280px-Oxf_ahoy_smollett_1751.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Oxf_ahoy_smollett_1751.jpg/500px-Oxf_ahoy_smollett_1751.jpg?utm_sour